What does this function return, and what are the list contents afterwards? The list is `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6` and `k = 3`.
```c
Node *rev(Node *head, int k) {
  Node *prev = NULL, *cur = head;
  while (cur && k--) {
    Node *nx = cur->next;
    cur->next = prev;
    prev = cur;
    cur = nx;
  }
  head->next = cur;
  return prev;
}
```

The list is `4 -> 9 -> 2 -> 7` with `head` at 4. What does this print, and what is the list afterwards?
```c
Node *p = head;
p = p->next;
p->next = p->next->next;
printf("%d", head->next->next->value);
```

A dummy node `dummy` sits before the list `3 -> 8 -> 6 -> 5 -> 2 -> 7`. What is the list after this loop?
```c
prev = &dummy;  cur = dummy.next;
while (cur) {
  if (cur->v % 2 == 0) prev->next = cur->next;
  else prev = cur;
  cur = cur->next;
}
```

